{"kind":"artifact","text":"Exact-head implementation artifact at stable path internal/apphost for the platform-tag correction of the custody lost-update repair, exact pushed head f7a06c25dda963332fa4e6d49f5fc304a8bb4d20 on branch request/custody-lost-update-current (one commit over quarantined 1b3f4f1d0860eadae17321a616e060a513b5b032). The change is exactly two build-tag lines: config_lock_unix.go now enumerates linux || darwin || freebsd || netbsd || openbsd || dragonfly || illumos || android || ios — the platforms whose syscall package provides Flock — and config_lock_other.go complements it, so Android and iOS hold the real advisory lock instead of falling to the no-locking refusal while solaris, aix, windows, plan9, js and wasip1 keep that loud refusal. Conditions met at this head: GOOS=android GOARCH=arm64 builds the whole module including mains; every internal package compiles for GOOS=ios GOARCH=arm64 including internal/apphost itself, which is what proves syscall.Flock compiles there (full ios binaries require external cgo linking on any head of this repo, identical at base 1b3f4f1d, no iphoneos SDK on this host); GOOS=solaris amd64, GOOS=aix ppc64 and GOOS=windows amd64 build through the fallback; go test ./... passes on darwin/arm64, with TestUpdateConfigSerialisesConcurrentGrants and TestUpdateConfigNoChangeWritesNothing green. This artifact is the implementation report for codex correction request #10663 under promise #10681; correction recorded for Codex ratification at #10682 per request #10675 before this publication.","body":{"branch":"request/custody-lost-update-current","conditions":"Android and iOS take the real advisory lock; solaris/aix/windows/plan9/js/wasip1 keep the loud refusal; GOOS=android arm64 builds the whole module; every internal package compiles for GOOS=ios arm64; solaris amd64, aix ppc64, windows amd64 build; go test ./... passes on darwin/arm64 with both custody tests green.","head":"f7a06c25dda963332fa4e6d49f5fc304a8bb4d20"}}